    ("GOAL_MAX_CONCURRENT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Max concurrent goal runs."),
    ("GOAL_FAIR_DISPATCH", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "Round-robin the ready queue across objectives instead of the global `priority DESC, created_at` order, so one objective's backlog cannot take every dispatch slot while its neighbours starve. Priority still decides who is served FIRST within a pass; throughput is unchanged when o…"),
    ("GOAL_PER_OBJECTIVE_CAP", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0` (disabled)", "OPTIONAL hard ceiling on concurrent goal runs belonging to ONE objective, on top of the round-robin. `0` (default) means no per-objective ceiling — the round-robin alone spreads the slots and never idles one. Set `1` to guarantee a stream can never hold two slots even when nothi…"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Goal-planner feature gate."),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_MIN_READY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Min ready goals before planner triggers."),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3600`", "Planner cooldown (seconds)."),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_HISTORY_N", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`10`", "Planner goal history window."),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_SCALING", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "ONE revert for the whole planner half of stream scaling (`GOAL_FAIR_DISPATCH` reverts the dispatch half). `=false` restores the pre-scaling planner byte-for-byte: the derived ready ceiling falls back to the fixed `PLANNER_READY_FLOOR` (5, the old \"Never exceed 5 ready goals tota…"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_GOALS_PER_RUN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3`", "Upper bound on goals ONE planner run may create (\"Create 1-N goals\" in the planner prompt). Deliberately does NOT scale with the objective count — raising it raises spend per run, not coverage; coverage comes from the starvation order and the ready ceiling."),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_READY_CEILING", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0` (derive)", "Ready-goal ceiling the planner is told to respect, and the thinness gate `_maybe_plan` uses. `0` derives it as `max(5, active_objective_count)`, so a 16-stream board is allowed 16 ready goals instead of the legacy hardcoded 5 — five ready goals cannot cover sixteen streams. Any…"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_MAX_SOCIAL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`1`", "How many goals in one planner run may carry the `twitter` tool. Was the hardcoded \"At most ONE goal may include 'twitter'\". Raise it only with the outbound send cap in mind — it multiplies posting volume, not coverage."),
    ("GOAL_DAILY_QUOTA", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`6`", "Max goal runs started per trailing 24h; <=0 disables."),
    ("GOAL_SELF_WAKE_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Goal-initiated self-wake re-entry — gates whether the dispatcher *attempts* delivery (`agents/task/goals/dispatcher.py::_self_wake`). Required combination: this alone is not sufficient — the delivery producer (`TaskAgent.deliver_self_wake`) separately no-ops unless `SELF_WAKE_EN…"),
    ("GOAL_NOTIFY_ON_DONE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "§3.4 SAFETY NET (demoted from unconditional push): tell the user when a background goal completes only when the agent itself said nothing during the run (`RunOutcome.user_messages` empty) — the agent's own `send_message` (delivered live via the §3.1 rail) is the primary channel.…"),
    ("GOAL_DEDUP_THRESHOLD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0.6`", "Goal dedup similarity threshold (0.0–1.0)."),
    ("AUTONOMY_HALT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the 031 owner pause record — read, never written. The ONE runtime pause state is `<data_dir>/AUTONOMY_PAUSE.json` (scopes `all`/`trading`/`streams`/`planner`/`cron`/`social`/`oversight`/`pings`, optional expiry, atomic, fail-closed: an unreadable record is a paus…"),
    ("TREASURY_ENTRY_PAUSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the owner pause record — the `trading` scope: refuse NEW treasury positions (any chain, any turn origin) while still allowing exits (sells to the chain's quote asset, revokes). Set it live with `polyrob autonomy pause trading` / `polyrob owner pause-entries` / `/…"),
    ("STREAM_SEEDING_PAUSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the owner pause record — the `streams` scope: refuse NEW seeds from an operator's stream manifest (the file `POLYROB_STREAMS_MANIFEST` names, else `<data_home>/streams/streams.yaml`) while live goals, ad-hoc goals and cron run on. Set it live with `polyrob autono…"),
    ("CURATOR_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "stale/archive unused authored skills (Phase 1, no LLM)."),
    ("CURATOR_INTERVAL_HOURS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`168`", "Curator tick interval (hours)."),
    ("CURATOR_STALE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30`", "Days unused before a skill is staled."),
    ("CURATOR_ARCHIVE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`90`", "Days before stale skill is archived."),
    ("SANDBOX_REAP_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "043 A8/A42: the ownership-keyed sandbox-container sweep (removes a persistent docker sandbox whose owning session is gone; hourly-ish, `_SANDBOX_REAP_INTERVAL_SEC`=900s) — distinct from the AGE-based cold-start `reap_orphans`, which never runs periodically. No-op unless persiste…"),
    ("INSIGHTS_TOOL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "W7: read-only authored-skill reuse-% `insights` action."),
    ("AGENT_STATUS_TOOL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "I-6: read-only `agent_status` introspection action — steps used/remaining, active tools, context-token usage, wallet + tenant ledger; every section fails soft independently."),
    ("AVATAR_TOOL_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "The read-only `agent_avatar` action: the agent's own instance, frozen Mindprint face (traits/seed) and voice signature, plus `attach=true` to copy `pfp.png` into the session workspace so `message(media_paths=[...])` can deliver it. Never generates, re-rolls, keeps or pushes — `p…"),
    ("LIVE_HEALTH_CONTEXT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`true`", "2026-08-28 status SSOT: at the first step of every turn the agent receives a `<live-health>` control note rendered from the SAME `core/status_snapshot.py` snapshot the owner's `/status` shows (credit sentinel, live provider, open asks, blocked goals, suppressed owner notices, de…"),
    ("VERIFY_BEFORE_DONE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "I-3 / H3 (dedup decision D1): when the run's action ledger shows a successful code edit (`str_replace`/`apply_patch`/`create_file`/`move_file`/`delete_file`) more recent than the last successful `run_tests` (or with no `run_tests` at all), the first `done()` is intercepted with…"),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_AUTOLOAD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "C9: auto-load a project file as a frozen `PROJECT_CONTEXT` foundation message. Names by precedence: `polyrob.md` > `POLYROB.md` > `AGENTS.md` > `CLAUDE.md` > `.cursorrules` (highest-precedence name that exists wins; not concatenated). Local = trusted/steering."),
    ("ENV_CONTEXT_BLOCK", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "014-C1: pin the `<environment>` foundation block (instance, platform, data dir, absolute workspace path + persistence semantics, posture axes, host-executable probe) so the agent knows where it lives. Emits ONLY under `POLYROB_LOCAL` or effective `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous` — a p…"),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_MAX_TOKENS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`20000`", "Token cap on concatenated project-context content (truncated with a notice)."),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_SERVER_MODE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (NOT a safe-local flag)", "Load project context on the server (not local mode) and inject it untrusted-wrapped (framed as DATA, not instructions). Searches the tenant session workspace (`pm().get_workspace_dir`), NEVER the process CWD/install dir. `POLYROB_LOCAL` does NOT flip this on."),
    ("EPISODIC_MEMORY_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED, or `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Episodic activity ledger: write one durable, time-ordered row per completed run (chat/goal/cron) to the `episodes` table in `memory.db`, independent of H-MEM findings. Feeds `recent_activity`, the session-start digest, and the continuity bridge."),
    ("EPISODIC_DIGEST_INJECT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED, or `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Inject a passive session-start digest of recent episodes (chat sessions only, `exclude_surfaced=True`) as a pinned foundation message."),
    ("CONTINUITY_BRIDGE_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Idle-reset continuity bridge: write a closing episode + seed the next session's first step with a short \"what happened last time\" bridge message."),
    ("AUTONOMOUS_CONTINUITY_BRIDGE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.5: carry a recent-activity summary INTO an autonomous goal/cron tick (mirror-image of the chat digest — autonomous-only, first-step, never sub-agent) so ticks stop re-deriving \"nothing new\". Additive context; fail-open."),
    ("SELF_EVOLUTION_TRANSPARENCY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "§7.1: proactively notify the owner (Telegram) when the agent writes a pending identity/skill proposal, and back the `polyrob owner pending/promote/reject` surface. Fail-open."),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKER_ESCALATION", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.2: when a goal trips the circuit breaker (`status='blocked'`) OR the planner leaves the pipeline empty repeatedly, surface a concrete ask to the owner over the cron/delivery telegram rail instead of dying silently; also leaves a tracked `kind='ask'` row on the goal board (`po…"),
    ("GOAL_EMPTY_PIPELINE_ESCALATE_AFTER", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Consecutive planner runs that leave the ready queue EMPTY before the stall is escalated to the owner (rides `GOAL_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`; a \"queue healthy\" planner verdict never escalates; escalates once per stall)."),
    ("GOAL_GROUP_MAX_REPLIES_PER_RUN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3`", "how many room lines ONE service run (a cron job or goal carrying `payload.group`) may answer. The run is told the number in its rubric and each answer is a `send_message(reply_to=<message id>)`. This is the per-RUN share of the room's hourly ceiling (`GROUP_REPLY_CAP_PER_HOUR`),…"),
    ("GOAL_COMPLETION_JUDGE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "§4.3 evidence-grounded completion review (autonomous runs): a cheap aux model (the `judge` aux slot) reads the agent's CLAIM (done() text) against the mechanical evidence pack — action ledger, artifact diff, captured ids, typed-check results — acceptance prose optional. `unmet`…"),
    ("GOAL_JUDGE_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`60`", "Wall-clock bound on one completion-judge LLM call; timeout fails open to pass."),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKED_MAX_AGE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`14`", "§5.3 blocked-goal stewardship: `blocked` goals older than this (measured from when they blocked) age out VISIBLY to `cancelled` (logged `aged_out` event) on the dispatch tick, instead of rotting as permanent planner context. `0` disables aging. The owner/agent can requeue a bloc…"),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKED_PROVIDER_RETRY_MIN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30` (minutes)", "For typed block kinds, a `blocked` goal whose `payload.block_kind == \"provider_outage\"` (stamped by `dispatcher._fail_run` when the failure classified as an LLM/provider death) is a transient, self-healing block — `age_out_blocked` requeues it (`blocked`→`ready` + `provider_outa…"),
    ("REFLECTION_ON_SESSION_CLOSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.7: consolidate a short session's findings at session close (the per-step 25-finding trigger is unreachable for short cron/goal sessions). Extra aux-model call per closed session."),
    ("AUTONOMY_STATE_DURABLE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "Restart-durable autonomy state (`autonomy_state.db`): background delegations write dispatched/terminal rows (a crash-interrupted delegation is marked `interrupted` at next start and surfaced back to its session — never silently resumed), and the self-wake `ReentryBudget` depth c…"),
    ("REFLECTION_SESSION_CLOSE_THRESHOLD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`5`", "Minimum findings a session must accrue for the `REFLECTION_ON_SESSION_CLOSE` trigger to fire (cost gate)."),
    ("CONTINUITY_LLM_SUMMARY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (everywhere; NOT a safe-local flag)", "Use an aux-model LLM call to summarize the closing episode for the continuity bridge instead of a mechanical summary. Off by default everywhere — adds latency at reset."),
    ("EPISODIC_RETENTION_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`90`", "Episodic row retention window (days). Enforced by a global (all-tenants) prune riding the curator's own tick cadence — never the write path."),
    ("AUTONOMY_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`300` (min 30)", "Interval of the autonomy runtime's heartbeat ticker (liveness stamp + event-log maintenance host)."),
    ("POLYROB_STREAMS_MANIFEST", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "unset (then `<data_home>/streams/streams.yaml` if it exists; no manifest ships)", "Path override for an operator-authored streams manifest the stream seeder loads. Nothing ships in the package; a fresh install has no standing work until an owner writes one. `load_manifest` refuses a path under a session workspace and the file is hard-denied to agent writes."),
    ("SUB_AGENTS_ENABLED", "Delegation / sub-agents", "**ON** (`'true'`; `BotConfig` field also `True`)", "Enable `delegate_task` / sub-agent delegation."),
    ("SUBAGENT_LEAST_PRIVILEGE", "Delegation / sub-agents", "ON (`'true'`)", "Give a delegated child a narrowed dedicated controller/toolset."),
    ("DELEGATE_BLOCKED_TOOLS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`{code_execution, coding, cronjob, git, github, hf_deploy, hyperliquid, mcp, polymarket, process, self_env, shell, tool_manage, x402_invoice, x402_pay}`", "Container tool_ids dropped from a delegated child. Default DERIVED from the capability table (`ids_with(\"delegate_blocked\")`). The env can only ADD — it is UNIONed with the default (M5, 2026-09-14: it used to REPLACE, so naming one extra tool silently unblocked every money tool…"),
    ("MAX_SUB_AGENT_DEPTH", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`1`", "Delegation depth backstop."),
    ("MAX_CONCURRENT_SUB_AGENTS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`3`", "Max concurrent sub-agents."),
    ("MAX_ASYNC_SUB_AGENTS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`2` (clamped ≤ concurrent)", "Background/async delegation slots."),
    ("SUB_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`600`", "Single sub-agent (`goal`) timeout."),
    ("SUB_AGENT_TIMEOUT", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`600`", "Single sub-agent (`goal`) timeout."),
    ("PARALLEL_SUBTASKS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`900`", "Parallel-subtasks timeout."),
    ("PARALLEL_SUBTASKS_TIMEOUT", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`900`", "Parallel-subtasks timeout."),
    ("WORKERS_ENABLED", "Delegation / sub-agents", "OFF", "043 §6 — arm the tenant-scoped worker (agent-profile) store. A \"worker\" is an `AgentProfileModel` (prompt/llm/tools/limits) authored per tenant under `<data_home>/profiles/user_{uid}/`, threat-scanned (body AND description separately, fail-CLOSED → `.pending/` quarantine), atomi…"),
    ("MCP_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`False`) (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Enable the MCP subsystem globally."),
    ("MAX_MCP_PER_STEP", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`3`", "Max MCP tool calls per step."),
    ("MCP_EXEC_RATE_PER_WINDOW", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`20`", "MCP exec rate-limit count per window."),
    ("MCP_EXEC_RATE_WINDOW_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`60`", "MCP exec rate-limit window (s)."),
    ("MCP_ENCRYPTION_KEY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Fernet key for MCP secret store."),
    ("MCP_OAUTH_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`False`)", "Inject OAuth `Authorization` headers into SSE/HTTP/streamable MCP server connections that declare an `auth: {provider: \"generic_oauth2\", ...}` block (`MCPServerConfig.auth`) — mints/refreshes the token via a persisted (`FileTokenStore`, Fernet-encrypted), lazily-built `OAuthMana…"),
    ("MCP_SELF_INSTALL_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`False`)", "Register the agent-callable `mcp_install` action (install a vetted catalog MCP server at runtime). Forged/autonomous turns always refused; approval is Deny-by-default unless `APPROVAL_PROVIDER` is set. NOT in the `POLYROB_LOCAL` safe group."),
    ("MCP_INSTALL_CATALOG_FILE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Path to a REVIEWED JSON file of extra installable catalog entries (`{\"<id>\": {description, transport, url/command, trust}}`), merged over the builtins (file wins on id clash). The real operator seam for extending the install catalog."),
    ("MCP_INSTALL_ALLOWLIST", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Comma list of extra ids admitted to the install allowlist. An id WITHOUT a catalog entry still has nothing to install — prefer `MCP_INSTALL_CATALOG_FILE`."),
    ("ANYSITE_TOOL_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`True`)", "Register the `anysite_api` CLI tool."),
    ("ANYSITE_API_KEY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "AnySite API credential."),
    ("CODING_TOOLS_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Register the coding tools (str_replace/grep/run_tests)."),
    ("CODING_LSP_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local)", "I-2 / H1 (dedup decision D2): after a successful `str_replace`/`apply_patch`/`create_file`, run an external checker (`pyright --outputjson` for `.py`, `tsc --noEmit` for `.ts`/`.tsx`/`.js`/`.jsx`) against the freshly-written file and append an errors-only `<diagnostics>` block t…"),
    ("CODING_SNAPSHOT_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local)", "I-4 / H2 (dedup decision D3): shadow-git PER-FILE snapshot/restore. Before each mutating coding action (`str_replace`/`apply_patch`/`move_file`/`delete_file`, and `create_file` only when overwriting an existing file), commit the SINGLE touched file into a shadow git repo under t…"),
    ("GIT_TOOLS_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Register the `git` tool (status/diff/log/branch/checkout/add/commit/pull/push/clone) over the confined workspace."),
    ("GITHUB_TOOL_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local; ON under `AGENT_BUILDER_MODE=build\\", "ship`)"),
    ("CODE_EXEC_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF", "Register `code_execution` tool (NOT a sandbox; never in default tool_ids)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_BACKEND", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`local_subprocess`", "Code-exec backend selector."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`30` (dev mode, unset: follows `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC`=300)", "Hard cap on a code-exec run. An explicit value always wins; unset under the docker backend's dev mode (posture ≥1) the cap follows `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC` so `run_code` and `shell_run` share ONE foreground ceiling."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`100000`", "Code-exec output byte cap."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_DOCKER_IMAGE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`python:3.12-slim`", "Container image for the `docker` code-exec backend (explicit value wins over `CODE_EXEC_DEV_IMAGE` in every mode)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_DEV_IMAGE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`nikolaik/python-nodejs:python3.11-nodejs20`", "Image for the posture≥1 persistent DEV container when `CODE_EXEC_DOCKER_IMAGE` is unset — python+node so npm/npx toolchains work (014 B1)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_NETWORK", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`none`", "Docker container network policy: `none` / `egress` (→ docker `bridge`) / `host`; unrecognized values fall back to `none`."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_CONTAINER_MEMORY_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`1024`", "Docker container memory cap (MB); also sets `--memory-swap` equal (no swap headroom)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_CONTAINER_CPUS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`1.0`", "Docker container CPU cap (`--cpus`)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_PIDS_LIMIT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`256`", "Docker container PID cap (`--pids-limit`)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SHM_SIZE_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`1024`", "Docker container `/dev/shm` size (MB, `--shm-size`). Docker's own default is 64MB regardless of `--memory` — too small for a real headless-Chromium render (Puppeteer/Playwright/Remotion mmap frame buffers there); a bare `chromium --headless` page fetch doesn't hit it, only an ac…"),
    ("CODE_EXEC_DOCKER_USER", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset → invoking uid:gid, or `65534:65534` (nobody:nogroup) when the host process itself runs as root", "Explicit override for the docker backend's `--user`."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_DOCKER_PERSISTENT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON at `AGENT_COMPUTE_POSTURE>=1`**)", "Opt-in: ONE persistent per-session `docker` container (`docker exec` per call) instead of a fresh ephemeral container per `run_code` call, so pip installs/cwd survive across calls within a session. Defaults ON at posture≥1 (sandbox-dev installs must persist); explicit value wins."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_PUBLISH_PORTS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`8000,5000,8080,3000`", "Container ports a dev (posture≥1) persistent sandbox publishes to host loopback (`-p 127.0.0.1::<port>`, docker-assigned host ports) so the agent can HTTP-test a server it started. Non-dev/ephemeral runs publish nothing."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SSH_HOST", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (required for `CODE_EXEC_BACKEND=ssh`)", "Remote host the `ssh` code-exec backend runs `run_code` on over the system `ssh` binary. `setup()` fails loudly if unset when `ssh` is selected; refused if the value begins with `-` (option-injection guard)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SSH_USER", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (omit `user@` — SSH client/`~/.ssh/config` default applies)", "SSH login user for the `ssh` code-exec backend. Refused if the value begins with `-`."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SSH_PORT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`22`", "SSH port for the `ssh` code-exec backend."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SSH_KEY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Identity file (`-i`) for the `ssh` code-exec backend. Never logged (only host/port/exit-code are logged; the full argv, which carries this path, is not)."),
    ("CODE_EXEC_SSH_SANDBOXED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`False`)", "Operator ATTESTATION that the `CODE_EXEC_SSH_HOST` remote is hardened/disposable, flipping the `ssh` backend's reported `capabilities[\"sandbox\"]` True. By default it is honestly `False` — a generic remote host is a different trust domain where agent code runs with the SSH user's…"),
    ("SHELL_TOOLS_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON at `AGENT_COMPUTE_POSTURE>=1`**)", "Register the persistent `shell` + `process` tools (run inside the session's sandbox container; cwd/env persist; background job manager). Every action is additionally `compute_posture_allows(ctx,1)`-gated (owner, not leaf/forged). In `DELEGATE_BLOCKED_TOOLS`; never in default too…"),
    ("SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`300`", "ONE foreground ceiling for the agent's build commands: `shell_run` clamps its `timeout` to it (120 when the agent omits `timeout`) and the docker backend's dev-mode `run_code` cap follows it when `CODE_EXEC_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC` is unset. Raised from the old 120 s literal (publishing…"),
    ("APP_SERVICE_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (ON under effective `AGENT_BUILDER_MODE=ship`)", "032: register the `app_service` tool (`deploy`/`stop`/`list_apps`/`logs`) and arm the owner-owned supervisor unit. Never in default `tool_ids`; a stream manifest or the owner grants it per goal. The agent only writes registry rows — `polyrob-apps.service` (`polyrob apps supervis…"),
    ("APP_SERVICE_ALLOW_PUBLIC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (ON under effective `AGENT_BUILDER_MODE=ship`)", "Render the public nginx stanza for a live app (`https://<slug>.<APP_SERVICE_BASE_DOMAIN>`). OFF ⇒ apps run on loopback only and `app_list` says so. NOT flipped by `POLYROB_LOCAL`."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_BASE_DOMAIN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "The wildcard base, e.g. `apps.example.com` (one `*.apps.example.com` certificate). Required for a public URL; without it `ship` mode clamps to `build`."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_MAX_LIVE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`3`", "Apps per tenant that may hold an address (approved/deploying/live/paused)."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_DAILY_MAX", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Deploy requests per tenant per rolling 24 h."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`120`", "Minimum seconds between deploy requests of ONE slug."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_MEMORY_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`512`", "Per-app container memory ceiling (memory == memory-swap)."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_CPUS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`0.5`", "Per-app CPU ceiling."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_PIDS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`256`", "Per-app pid ceiling."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_SNAPSHOT_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`500`", "Cap on the tested-tree snapshot an app runs from (symlinks, `.git`, caches and credential files are never copied)."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_EGRESS_DEFAULT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`none`", "Egress when the verb omits it: `none` (deny all but replies) \\"),
    ("APP_SERVICE_PORT_RANGE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`18000-18099`", "Loopback host ports the supervisor allocates from (the agent never chooses a port)."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_TICK_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`30`", "Supervisor reconcile cadence (also the pause-edge latency for live apps)."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_HEALTH_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`90`", "Time to the first healthy `health_path` response before a deploy is `failed`."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_IMAGE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`CODE_EXEC_DEV_IMAGE` else `polyrob-dev:latest`", "Base image an app container runs in."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_RETAIN_DAYS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`7`", "Days a stopped/failed app's snapshot is kept before pruning."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_CERT_DIR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`/etc/letsencrypt/live/<APP_SERVICE_BASE_DOMAIN>`", "Directory holding the wildcard `fullchain.pem`/`privkey.pem` the stanzas reference."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_NGINX_CONF_DIR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`/etc/nginx/apps.d`", "Where the supervisor writes one `<slug>.conf` per live app. Your wildcard nginx server block must `include` this directory."),
    ("APP_SERVICE_SOURCE_ROOT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "An extra directory (beyond the data home and the supervisor's cwd) an app's source dir may live under; the supervisor refuses to snapshot from anywhere else."),
    ("APP_SERVICES_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/app_services.db`", "Override for the app registry DB (tests redirect it per test)."),
    ("AGENT_BUILDER_MODE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`off`", "The FIFTH named default bundle (032; the `AUTONOMY_MODE` precedent): `off` = byte-identical; `build` = `PUBLISH_ENABLED` + `GITHUB_TOOL_ENABLED` default ON and `publish` joins the autonomous goal toolset; `ship` = `build` + `APP_SERVICE_ENABLED` + `APP_SERVICE_ALLOW_PUBLIC` ON a…"),
    ("SELF_ENV_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON at `AGENT_COMPUTE_POSTURE>=2`**)", "Register the `self_env` self-maintenance tool (install_dep/read_source/patch_source/git_pull/restart_service). Every verb is `compute_posture_allows(ctx,2)`- AND approval-gated; install-tree-confined; env/config hard-denied. In `DELEGATE_BLOCKED_TOOLS`."),
    ("POLYROB_INSTALL_TREE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "repo root (2 levels up from `tools/self_env/tool.py`)", "The install-tree root `self_env` read/patch/git_pull operate under (realpath-confined). Set to `/opt/polyrob` on prod."),
    ("POLYROB_SUPERVISED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF", "Assert a supervisor (e.g. systemd `Restart=`) will respawn the process, so `self_env_restart_service` may request a restart. Unset = restart refused (never kill an unsupervised agent)."),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local)", "Register the `hf_deploy` tool (deploy/undeploy/list_deployments — publish the session workspace as a Hugging Face Space, Docker SDK). Requires `compute_posture_allows(ctx,2)`. The FIRST publish of a new app is gated by a real approving provider — the tool resolves the same inter…"),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_ORG", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "The Hugging Face org/user namespace to publish Spaces under (`<HF_DEPLOY_ORG>/<app_name>`). Required for `deploy`/`undeploy`; refused with a clear error when unset."),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_DAILY_MAX", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Max deploy attempts per tenant per rolling 24h."),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`120`", "Minimum seconds between deploy attempts of the SAME app."),
    ("OBJECTIVE_GOAL_BUDGET", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`25`", "Max LIVE (non-cancelled) goals one objective may have attached. Past the cap `GoalBoard.create` REFUSES a new child with a message telling the agent to finish/cancel open goals or raise an ask instead — an objective is allowed to be standing, not infinite. An objective's own `pa…"),
    ("PUBLISH_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local; ON under `AGENT_BUILDER_MODE=build\\", "ship`)"),
    ("PUBLISH_ROOT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_home>/publish`", "Directory the web server serves publications from. Approved slugs live at `<PUBLISH_ROOT>/<slug>/`; unapproved ones wait under `<PUBLISH_ROOT>/.pending/<slug>/`, which is not a valid slug and so is unreachable — the approval gate is enforced by the filesystem layout, not by appl…"),
    ("PUBLISH_BASE_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (relative URLs)", "Public base URL that serves `PUBLISH_ROOT` (e.g. `https://pub.example.com`). The `publish` tool returns `<PUBLISH_BASE_URL>/<slug>/`; unset yields a relative `/<slug>/`, which is honest but not shareable. Set it to the public vhost that serves `PUBLISH_ROOT`."),
    ("PUBLICATIONS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/publications.db`", "Override the publications DB location (slug → status/url/size). Mainly a test seam."),
    ("ARTIFACTS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/artifacts.db`", "Override the artifact-ledger DB location (one row per file the agent produces: producer, path, sha256, size, kind, published url). Mainly a test seam."),
    ("HF_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret)", "Hugging Face fine-grained write token used ONLY by the `hf_deploy` broker (`HfApi`) to create/update Spaces and set secrets; read+stripped at call time, never logged/returned (broker errors are token-scrubbed). See the owner runbook in `docs/guide/self-hosting.md`."),
    ("DEPLOYED_APPS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (derived from data root)", "Override path for the `hf_deploy` registry DB (`deployed_apps.db`); the test suite redirects this to keep unit runs off the developer's real data home."),
    ("CRON_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF", "Register the `cronjob` tool + start the cron ticker."),
    ("WAKE_CHANGE_GATE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE=full`**)", "Cron wake change-gate: a job with `payload.change_gated` skips the paid model call ($0 tick, `cron_run skipped/no_change`) when the tenant's observable state fingerprint (goal board/events, other cron runs, newest episode) is unchanged since the last tick. Delivery jobs (`payloa…"),
    ("MESSAGE_TOOL_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Agent-callable `message(surface, target, text, action)` send tool. Every non-owner target is default-DENIED unless owner-allowlisted (`polyrob owner allow <surface> <target>` / Telegram `/allow`). ⚠️ Owner-target resolution reads the single process-level operator env (`POLYROB_O…"),
    ("MESSAGE_AUTONOMOUS_ALLOWLISTED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Whether a forged/AUTONOMOUS turn (goal/cron/planner session, sub-agent, self-wake re-entry) may use `message` at all. OFF = blanket refusal (\"owner must be in the loop\"). ON = the send falls through to the normal tier gate, so an autonomous run can reach ONLY the owner or an own…"),
    ("OWNER_MESSAGE_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`7200` (2h)", "Minimum gap an autonomous/forged turn (goal/cron/planner session, sub-agent, self-wake re-entry) must respect before proactively messaging the OWNER again — checked against the durable conversation store's REAL send history, never the model's own self-report of elapsed time. `<=…"),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Goal/cron completion pushes attach the run's file deliverables (screened + capped) to the OWNER chat via the delivery rail; the honest text listing (`attached` / `server-only: <path> (<reason>)`) rides regardless. Owner rail only — correspondents never receive workspace files."),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Per-file attach cap in MB for the completion AUTO-attach (Telegram bot API hard limit is 50). Oversized files are listed server-only, never silently dropped. The explicit `message` tool rides the larger `MESSAGE_MEDIA_MAX_MB` instead."),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_MAX_FILES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`3`", "Max files attached to one completion message; the remainder is listed by name+size+path."),
    ("DELIVERABLES_MAX_LINES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`5`", "UNCONDITIONAL cap on individually-listed deliverable lines in one owner message; everything past it becomes ONE roll-up line plus the console link (chat-first review 2026-08-22, G1/G4). Attached and published files are never rolled up. This bound does NOT depend on ledger attrib…"),
    ("MESSAGE_MEDIA_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`45`", "Per-file cap for the explicit `message` tool `media_paths` send (owner-directed; Telegram hard limit ~50 MB). The full attach screen (confinement, secret filename+content, injection scan) applies regardless of cap."),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON", "Master switch for the INBOUND media rail: a photo/document/video arriving on a chat surface is stored in the session workspace under `inbound/` and described on the turn (image ⇒ a vision block, small text file ⇒ inlined, anything else ⇒ referenced by path). OFF = the pre-2026-0…"),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`20`", "Per-file cap for a file arriving from a chat surface. Over the cap the file is not stored and the turn says so."),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_MAX_FILES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`5`", "Max attachments read from ONE inbound message; the remainder is counted on the turn (\"N more attachment(s) … were not read\"), never dropped in silence."),
    ("INBOUND_IMAGE_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Per-image cap for building a vision block (base64 inflates ~33%). Over the cap the image IS stored and its path named, but no vision block is built — the agent is told to say so rather than guess."),
    ("WEBVIEW_PUBLIC_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Public base URL of the owner-auth webview console (e.g. `https://console.example.com`). Set ⇒ goal completions carry a `/session/<id>` deep link and the daily digest a console line; unset ⇒ no links (byte-identical). Links carry no credentials — the console's own owner login gat…"),
    ("APPROVAL_REQUIRED_TOOLS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`''` (no-op)", "Comma list of tools requiring approval before execution."),
    ("APPROVAL_PROVIDER", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`auto`", "Approval provider: `auto`(allow)/`auto_notify`(allow + `tool_auto_approved` audit event + post-hoc owner notification — act-and-report)/`deny`/custom (`interactive_cli`, `owner_queue` self-register on import). Under effective `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous` an unset/`auto`/`interacti…"),
    ("APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`30`", "Approval-request timeout (cancels provider on expiry). The generic 30s default applies only to in-process providers; every durable `owner_queue` wait (payment lanes AND the non-payment queued lanes, 030 WS-E2) defaults to the remote-round-trip 300s via `approval_wait_timeout_sec…"),
    ("PAYMENT_APPROVAL_MODE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`approve` (`auto` under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "the owner-legible switch for outward payment-creation actions (`PAYMENT_APPROVAL_TOOLS`), gated FIRST-CLASS independent of `APPROVAL_REQUIRED_TOOLS`. `approve`: every request (receive AND spend) queues through the durable, remote-capable `owner_queue` provider (`tools/controller…"),
    ("APPROVAL_GRANT_TTL_HOURS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`24`", "TTL for an `owner_queue` ONE-SHOT grant: an owner decision recorded AFTER the requester already timed out still lets the NEXT identical request (same tool+params+tenant hash) through without re-queuing — but only within this window, and only once (atomic single redemption via `G…"),
    ("POLYROB_TOOL_DENYLIST", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`''`", "Comma list of tools vetoed by the pre-tool-call guardrail (fail-closed)."),
    ("POLYROB_AGENT_TOOLSET", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Named toolset driving the CLI session's tool list (`resolve_toolset`), same as `polyrob run --toolset <name>`. Unset ⇒ the legacy CLI default list (`filesystem`/`task`/`web_fetch` + gated `coding`/`anysite`). Either way the list is intersected with `cli_unavailable_tools` so unr…"),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMA_ERROR_POLICY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`DROP_TOOL`", "Invalid native schema handling: `DROP_TOOL`/`RAISE`/`WARN`."),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMA_SANITIZE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`'true'`)", "Fix hostile JSON-Schema constructs in the emitted tools list."),
    ("UNTRUSTED_TOOL_RESULT_WRAP", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "**ON**", "Frame untrusted tool-result strings in `<untrusted_tool_result>` delimiters."),
    ("ENABLE_GIF_CREATION", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF", "(Legacy/dead) GIF creation."),
    ("FS_REALPATH_CONFINE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`\"on\"`)", "Confine filesystem ops via realpath."),
    ("BROWSER_ALLOW_PRIVATE_URLS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Allow browser navigation to private/loopback URLs."),
    ("BROWSER_CDP_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Chrome DevTools Protocol endpoint of a browser running as its OWN principal (`polyrob browser install` → `polyrob-browser.service`, `http://127.0.0.1:9222`). REQUIRED once the wallet is enabled: a custody process refuses to launch Chromium and only connects. Every session gets a…"),
    ("BROWSER_WSS_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Playwright-server WebSocket endpoint of a remote browser (`ws://<private-ip>:3000/<token>`), for a browser on a SECOND host; requires the same Playwright version on both ends. Preferred over CDP across a network (CDP has no authentication). Same fresh-context and never-rendered…"),
    ("GIT_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`120`", "Per-command subprocess timeout (seconds) for the `git` tool."),
    ("GITHUB_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret, masked)", "GitHub token for the `github` tool when no per-user OAuth token is stored (`GITHUB_TOKEN` wins; the standard gh-CLI/Actions names)."),
    ("GH_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret, masked)", "GitHub token for the `github` tool when no per-user OAuth token is stored (`GITHUB_TOKEN` wins; the standard gh-CLI/Actions names)."),
    ("TWITTER_WRITE_MAX_PER_HOUR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`15`", "Sliding-window cap on `x_browser` posts and DM sends per account/action bucket."),
    ("OPENAI_COMPAT_API_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "OFF", "Mount the OpenAI-compatible `/v1` router. On `/v1`, the request `body.model` (which OpenAI SDK clients always send) is applied per-session and overrides the operator's `CHAT_MODEL`/`CHAT_PROVIDER` pin for that session (live `swap_model` on a reused session; baked into the Sessio…"),
    ("MCP_SERVE_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "OFF", "Mount the inbound MCP server surface — `POST /mcp`, hand-rolled JSON-RPC-over-POST (not the `mcp` PyPI SDK), auth via the same `X-API-KEY`/JWT/x402 policy as A2A. Lets an MCP client (Claude Desktop, Cursor) call five tenant-safe read-only tools (`rob_usage_summary`, `rob_goals_l…"),
    ("SESSION_REGISTRY_BACKEND", "API / server / sessions", "`memory`", "Active session→orchestrator map backend: `memory` (in-proc) or `sqlite` (cross-proc metadata). ⚠️ `sqlite` on BOTH units is the precondition for a WRITABLE console (`WEBVIEW_READ_ONLY=false`): with `memory` the console's own in-process agent cannot see the sessions the agent ser…"),
    ("API_HOST", "API / server / sessions", "`127.0.0.1`", "API bind host."),
    ("API_PORT", "API / server / sessions", "`9000`", "API bind port."),
    ("API_AUTH_TOKEN", "API / server / sessions", "unset", "API auth token."),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_RPM", "API / server / sessions", "`60`", "API requests/minute."),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_RPH", "API / server / sessions", "`1000`", "API requests/hour."),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_BURST", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "API burst allowance."),
    ("CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS", "API / server / sessions", "**Two independent consumers, two different defaults** — see note below", "Comma-separated allowed CORS origins."),
    ("WEBVIEW_DOMAIN", "API / server / sessions", "the reference deployment's public host (`webview/server.py`, `api/auth_endpoints.py`); `localhost:5050` (`agents/task/utils_webview.py`) — **inconsistent default across call sites; set `WEBVIEW_DOMAIN` for your own deployment**", "The public hostname this instance is served from. Feeds the Socket.IO CORS default (below) and the SIWE `domain` field (`api/auth_endpoints.py:108`)."),
    ("JWT_SECRET_KEY", "API / server / sessions", "unset (dev)", "JWT signing secret, shared by the API auth middlewares and the WebView (`webview/owner_auth.py` issues/verifies the owner session cookie with the same secret). Required in production — `api/app.py` raises `RuntimeError` at startup if unset and `ENVIRONMENT=production`; in dev, u…"),
    ("A2A_BASE_URL", "API / server / sessions", "the reference deployment's base URL (set this to your own public URL)", "Base URL advertised in the A2A agent card."),
    ("WEBVIEW_ACTIVITY_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "`true`", "The console's global `/activity` stream (page + `/api/activity/*` + `join_activity` socket room). Owner/admin-gated in every non-local posture, so on-by-default is safe; `false` = 404/denied everywhere."),
    ("WEBVIEW_ACTIVITY_TAIL_SEC", "API / server / sessions", "`2.0`", "Poll interval for the activity hub's SQLite id-cursor tails (`telemetry_events.db`, `goal_events`, `skill_install_audit`). Feed events are push (watchfiles), not polled."),
    ("WEBVIEW_READ_ONLY", "API / server / sessions", "`false`", "Monitoring-only console: every mutating endpoint returns 403 server-side through ONE dependency (`webgate.read_only_guard`; the auth surfaces `/owner-login` and `/api/auth/*` stay reachable so the owner can still log in to LOOK) and the chat input is not rendered. The posture fo…"),
    ("POLYROB_API_BASE", "API / server / sessions", "`http://127.0.0.1:9000`", "Base URL of the main task API the webview proxies to (chat delivery, queue-status, health) in the classic two-service shape. Override for a non-default API port/host."),
    ("SESSION_TTL_SECONDS", "API / server / sessions", "`86400`", "Session lifetime."),
    ("MAX_SESSIONS_IN_MEMORY", "API / server / sessions", "`100`", "Resident session cap."),
    ("MAX_SESSIONS_PER_USER", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "Per-user session cap."),
    ("CREATED_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS", "API / server / sessions", "`3600`", "TTL for a created-but-not-yet-run session."),
    ("SESSION_RESET_MODE", "API / server / sessions", "`idle` (#7)", "Chat session-boundary policy: `idle`/`daily`/`both`/`none`. Default `idle` everywhere — a chat idle past `SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES` starts fresh (memory recall bridges the gap). The server flip (was `none`) is gated on the recreate-race (#2) + mute-on-resume (#0) fixes. Pin `none` f…"),
    ("SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES", "API / server / sessions", "`1440` (**720 POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Idle threshold; a chat idle longer than this starts a fresh session (when `SESSION_RESET_MODE` includes idle). Last-activity is bumped per message via `SessionChatRegistry.touch`."),
    ("SESSION_RESET_HOUR", "API / server / sessions", "`4`", "Local hour (0-23) for the daily session roll (when mode includes daily)."),
    ("SURFACE_GC_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "ON when local **+** chat bus on, else OFF", "Periodic GC (hourly via the autonomy runtime) of stale chat<->session bindings; horizon `max(2× idle window, 7d)`. Keeps the routing map from growing unboundedly."),
    ("UVICORN_HOST", "API / server / sessions", "`127.0.0.1`", "Uvicorn bind host (read in `main.py`)."),
    ("UVICORN_PORT", "API / server / sessions", "`9000`", "Uvicorn bind port (read in `main.py`)."),
    ("UVICORN_WORKERS", "API / server / sessions", "`1`", "Uvicorn worker count (read in `main.py`)."),
    ("UVICORN_RELOAD", "API / server / sessions", "OFF (`false`)", "Uvicorn auto-reload (read in `main.py`)."),
    ("ENVIRONMENT", "API / server / sessions", "`development` (varies by site)", "Environment selector."),
    ("ENV", "API / server / sessions", "`development` (varies by site)", "Environment selector."),
    ("LOG_LEVEL", "API / server / sessions", "`INFO`", "Logging level."),
    ("CHAT_TOOL_IDS", "API / server / sessions", "`task`", "Tools loaded for the chat surface."),
    ("CHAT_MAX_STEPS", "API / server / sessions", "`8`", "Max agent steps for a chat-surface turn."),
    ("RUN_BUDGET_USD", "API / server / sessions", "`0` (disabled)", "Session-cumulative provider-spend ceiling in USD; when > 0 the run loop halts honestly (`run_budget_exhausted`) before the next step once summed `usage_records.api_cost_usd` for the session reaches the cap. Real provider cost, not the markup user price. Sub-agents ride the paren…"),
    ("CHAT_SKIP_CREDIT_CHECK", "API / server / sessions", "ON (truthy)", "Skip the credit check on chat-path turns."),
    ("API_SECRET", "API / server / sessions", "unset (secret, masked)", "Secret key for the legacy `AuthenticationMiddleware` on the API app (`API_SECRET` wins, `ADMIN_TOKEN` is the fallback name); unset = that middleware is not added."),
    ("ADMIN_TOKEN", "API / server / sessions", "unset (secret, masked)", "Secret key for the legacy `AuthenticationMiddleware` on the API app (`API_SECRET` wins, `ADMIN_TOKEN` is the fallback name); unset = that middleware is not added."),
    ("PRODUCTION", "API / server / sessions", "OFF (`'true'` enables)", "Marks the deploy as production independent of `ENV`: a missing `JWT_SECRET_KEY` then becomes a fatal startup error instead of a dev warning."),
    ("MAX_CONCURRENT_UPDATES", "API / server / sessions", "`50`", "Semaphore bound on concurrent session-update operations in the API app."),
    ("SESSION_LLM_LIMIT", "API / server / sessions", "`5` (min 1)", "Per-session concurrent-LLM-call semaphore in the orchestrator."),
    ("MAX_QUEUED_MESSAGES", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "Per-session HITL inbound message queue bound (overflow is refused)."),
    ("POLYROB_LOCAL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Single-user terminal profile; flips the `_SAFE_LOCAL_FLAGS` group ON as a default."),
    ("ROB_LOCAL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Legacy alias for `POLYROB_LOCAL` (either being truthy enables local mode), kept so old docs/env files are not a silent no-op."),
    ("POLYROB_DATA_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Isolation switch (doc 01/06): when set — the headless/server case — the runtime data home (goals.db/cron.db/memory.db + agent workspaces) lives THERE, OUTSIDE the code tree, and the workspace is under it (not cwd). Unset (local-dev) keeps `cwd/.polyrob` as the data home, workspa…"),
    ("POLYROB_PROJECT_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "When set, the agent uses this folder as ONE persistent workspace shared across sessions/goals/cron (Claude-Code style), independent of `POLYROB_DATA_DIR`. Also via `polyrob --project <path>`. Goal concurrency is clamped to single-flight while active; the cross-process lock keys…"),
    ("POLYROB_LOG_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Runtime log directory override. Unset → `<data_home>/logs`; it never writes into the installed code tree. Never CWD-relative."),
    ("POLYROB_PROJECT_SECRET_REFUSE", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`0`", "When truthy, refuse to start if the cwd-default persistent workspace contains secrets/`.git` (SEC-1). Default = warn only."),
    ("POLYROB_REQUIRE_PAIRING", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Owner-allowlist + DM-pairing ingress gate; when ON, an unpaired sender is denied at the surface dispatcher."),
    ("TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Telegram bot token (from @BotFather) for the `polyrob telegram` local-polling surface. Read from process env or `./.polyrob/.env`; never commit it."),
    ("ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_IDS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Comma list of raw Telegram numeric user ids allowed to drive the bot. Unset ⇒ bot is locked and replies with the sender's id (bootstrap); set ⇒ only those ids reach the agent, others are ignored. A single entry here also serves as the owner tg id when `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`…"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's raw Telegram numeric id, used for two things: (1) the inbound owner alias — an inbound from this id is aliased to the OWNER principal (`POLYROB_OWNER_USER_ID`) instead of its surface-hashed `u_…` id, so the owner's chat shares autonomy's tenant (goals/memory/SELF); (…"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's email address for out-of-band cron delivery (`deliver=\"email\"`) on single-owner headless deploys where no `user_directory` service is registered. Mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`. Unset ⇒ email delivery has no recipient (fail-open, no send). Requires `CRON_DELIVER…"),
    ("BOT_OWNER_EMAIL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's email address for out-of-band cron delivery (`deliver=\"email\"`) on single-owner headless deploys where no `user_directory` service is registered. Mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`. Unset ⇒ email delivery has no recipient (fail-open, no send). Requires `CRON_DELIVER…"),
    ("OWNER_SURFACE", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (= `telegram`)", "030 WS-B1: the owner-notice fan-out order for `deliver_user_message` (approvals, credit sentinel, goal-blocked, settlement, cron reports) — a comma list of surface ids, primary first (e.g. `slack,telegram`). Each entry resolves an address via `owner_address()` (user_directory →…"),
    ("OWNER_SURFACES", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (= `telegram`)", "030 WS-B1: the owner-notice fan-out order for `deliver_user_message` (approvals, credit sentinel, goal-blocked, settlement, cron reports) — a comma list of surface ids, primary first (e.g. `slack,telegram`). Each entry resolves an address via `owner_address()` (user_directory →…"),
    ("OWNER_SLACK_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). Unset ⇒ that surface is unreachable for owner notices and the chain falls through."),
    ("OWNER_DISCORD_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). Unset ⇒ that surface is unreachable for owner notices and the chain falls through."),
    ("OWNER_SIGNAL_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). Unset ⇒ that surface is unreachable for owner notices and the chain falls through."),
    ("OWNER_WHATSAPP_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). Unset ⇒ that surface is unreachable for owner notices and the chain falls through."),
    ("OWNER_X_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). Unset ⇒ that surface is unreachable for owner notices and the chain falls through."),
    ("SINGULAR_CHAT_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for every `polyrob <surface>` daemon and `polyrob gateway`**)", "Installs the outbound surface bus so agent replies route to a chat surface."),
    ("TELEGRAM_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob telegram`**)", "Telegram surface enable flag."),
    ("DISCORD_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob discord`**)", "Discord surface enable flag (Gateway WS bot; DMs + allowlisted guild channels). Token via `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN`. ⚠️ The Message Content Intent must be enabled in the Discord developer portal (Bot → Privileged Gateway Intents) — without it guild messages arrive with EMPTY `content`…"),
    ("SLACK_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob slack`**)", "Slack surface enable flag (Socket Mode — no public URL). Tokens via `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` (xoxb-) + `SLACK_APP_TOKEN` (xapp-)."),
    ("SIGNAL_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob signal`**)", "Signal surface enable flag (local `signal-cli daemon --http`). Config via `SIGNAL_DAEMON_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8080`) + `SIGNAL_ACCOUNT` (+E164); `SIGNAL_SEND_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC` (default `1.0`) throttles sends."),
    ("X_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob x`**)", "X (Twitter) DM surface enable flag. Inbound = polling `GET /2/dm_events` (no DM webhook on the pay-per-use tier); outbound = `POST /2/dm_conversations/with/:participant_id/messages`. Creds are the SAME OAuth 1.0a user-context `TWITTER_*` env vars the twitter tool uses (bearer-on…"),
    ("X_DM_POLL_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`90`", "Seconds between `dm_events` polls. X allows 15 DM reads / 15 min per user (shared across DM GET endpoints), so 60s sits exactly at the cap with no pagination headroom; 90s (10/15 min) leaves room. A 429 backs off to the `x-rate-limit-reset` epoch regardless of this value. Sends…"),
    ("GROUP_CHAT_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Group/channel ingress. When ON: only chats in the default-DENY group allowlist (`polyrob owner groups allow <surface> <chat_id>`) are served; the owner keeps the normal flow (mention-gated); any other member's @mention routes as untrusted DATA into the bound group session (corre…"),
    ("GROUP_DEFAULT_MODE", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`mention`", "the default `chat.mode` for a room with no per-chat overlay. ADDRESSED = an @mention (or `text_mention`/`/cmd@bot`), a reply to one of the agent's own messages, or a `chat.wake_words` hit. `mention` = answer an ADDRESSED line from anyone — the owner is not exempt; `active` = ans…"),
    ("GROUP_REQUIRE_MENTION", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON", "Alias, one release. This flag was replaced this gate with `chat.mode`: `false` now means `GROUP_DEFAULT_MODE=active` (answer every message in an allowlisted room) and is resolved inside `ChatPolicy.defaults()`; an explicit `GROUP_DEFAULT_MODE` wins over it. Nothing else reads th…"),
    ("GROUP_TURN_TOOLS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "task,web_fetch,defi_data", "044: the read-only toolset of EVERY room-bound (public) session, owner included. A money/exec/delegate-blocked id, OR any other `high_impact` id (e.g. `browser`, `email`, `twitter`, `goal`) EXCEPT `web_fetch` — the room's designated already-untrusted-wrapped read tool — is dropp…"),
    ("GROUP_REPLY_CAP_PER_HOUR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "max committed replies `MessageRouter.publish` sends into one room chat per rolling hour; over cap the reply is suppressed (logged, never queued) and never counted twice. Read via a COUNT over `room_events`, so a restart can't reset it. DMs are never gated. A room that sets `chat…"),
    ("GROUP_MEMBER_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "minimum seconds between two triggers from the SAME sender (human or bot) in one room chat; a trigger inside the window is refused (`route_inbound` DENIED, silent). A room that sets `chat.member_cooldown_sec` overrides this for itself; `0` disables the cooldown for that room."),
    ("GROUP_BOT_LOOP_MAX", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "max bot-authored triggers allowed in one room chat within `GROUP_BOT_LOOP_WINDOW_SEC`; the limit-th+ trip records a `bot_loop_trip` and every further bot trigger is refused until `GROUP_BOT_LOOP_COOLDOWN_SEC` elapses. Humans are never counted here."),
    ("GROUP_BOT_LOOP_WINDOW_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`300`", "the rolling window `GROUP_BOT_LOOP_MAX` counts bot triggers over."),
    ("GROUP_BOT_LOOP_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`600`", "once the bot-loop guard trips, how long every bot trigger in that room chat is refused before the guard re-arms."),
    ("GROUP_LEDGER_MAX_ROWS_PER_CHAT", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`2000`", "max rows `group_ledger` retains per `(surface, chat_id)`; on every `append` the oldest rows beyond this count are deleted (newest kept)."),
    ("GROUP_LEDGER_RETENTION_DAYS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`14`", "wall-clock age window `group_ledger` retains per chat; a row older than `time.time() - GROUP_LEDGER_RETENTION_DAYS*86400` is deleted on the next `append` (prune-on-append) and cannot be read back even without one, since `tail` also prunes on every read (prune-on-read) — so a cha…"),
    ("TELEGRAM_INCREMENTAL_STREAM", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Live `editMessageText` streaming (#8): a turn's deltas open+edit one message (stable per-turn `stream_id`); the discrete reply finalizes that bubble in place via `_finalize_live_on_send` (clean final, no duplicate). Engine is in the base `Surface`; Telegram supplies the transpor…"),
    ("TELEGRAM_STREAM_EDIT_INTERVAL_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`1.5`", "Min seconds between live stream edits (flood-control); `0` edits on every delta."),
    ("VOICE_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Transcribe inbound voice/audio to text before routing (#9), so a voice note is handled like a typed message. Needs the faster-whisper extra; degrades to no-transcript if absent."),
    ("VOICE_TRANSCRIPT_ECHO", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON", "Echo the transcript back into the chat as a persistent, voice-note-anchored message (`🎙️ Transcript: \"…\"`) before the agent answers, on Telegram and WhatsApp. WhatsApp additionally marks the voice note read (✓✓). `false` = byte-identical prior behavior."),
    ("VOICE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`base`", "faster-whisper model size (`tiny`/`base`/`small`/`medium`/`large-v3`)."),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_ACCESS_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "The four-tier access model — the single switch for the whole feature (no sub-flags). When ON, `route_inbound` classifies each inbound as OWNER (steers), CORRESPONDENT (reply = DATA into the originating session via a `CORRESPONDENT`-origin control message, never a command), GROUP…"),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_REQUIRE_APPROVAL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`True`) (OFF under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "A newly auto-seeded correspondent is PENDING (owner must `polyrob owner approve`) before replies route. Set `false` for single-user/local."),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_MAX_NEW_PER_DAY", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "Per-tenant cap on new correspondents seeded per 24h (bounds injected mass-contact). Applies to genuinely NEW addresses only — idempotent re-seeds and thread-anchor rows (`provenance='thread'`) are exempt. Since 2026-07-13 the seed runs BEFORE the send and a cap-refusal blocks th…"),
    ("OUTBOUND_POLICY", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`allowlist` (`open` under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "pure outbound-policy model (`open\\"),
    ("OUTBOUND_DOMAINS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (empty)", "Comma-separated domain allowlist consulted when `OUTBOUND_POLICY=domains` (email-shaped targets only; other surfaces fall back to the exact-address allowlist). Merges with the guarded `outbound.domains` pref via `narrow_list` (allowlist polarity): the pref can only NARROW this s…"),
    ("OUTBOUND_DAILY_SEND_CAP", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`30`", "Control-plane cap on outbound sends/day once policy is `open`/`domains` (mirrors the `USER_DELIVERY_DAILY_CAP` convention). Guarded pref `outbound.daily_send_cap` merges via `min`. Landed as a `core/prefs.py` row in this task; enforcement is a separate task."),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_TTL_DAYS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`0` (never)", "Days of inactivity before a correspondent binding is marked expired (stops resolving). `0` = never — expiry silently breaks reply routing for long-quiet contacts, so it is an explicit opt-in. When >0, the hourly surface GC ticker runs `purge_expired`."),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_RESOLVE_LATEST", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`True`)", "When ONE tenant has several active bindings for one address (multiple sessions contacted the same person) and a reply carries no usable thread anchor, route it to the most recently active binding instead of quarantining. Cross-tenant ambiguity ALWAYS denies regardless. `false` =…"),
    ("CONVERSATION_RESUME_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`True`)", "When a correspondent replies to a conversation whose originating session is dead (missing/unrecreatable), create a replacement session seeded with the durable conversation context and re-point the bindings — instead of silently dropping their message (`correspondent_resumed` eve…"),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_REPLY_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "D1 scoped reply-while-tainted: permit `message`/`send_email` to EXACTLY the tainting (surface, address) — 1:1 only (multi-recipient/cc/bcc never exempt), rounds-capped, fail-closed. Default OFF keeps the owner-in-the-loop-per-round posture; every other high-impact tool stays blo…"),
    ("CORRESPONDENT_REPLY_MAX_ROUNDS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`5`", "Outbound messages per correspondent per 24h allowed under the scoped tainted-reply exemption (counted from the ConversationStore)."),
    ("MAX_EPHEMERAL_MESSAGES", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`30`", "Cap on the one-shot ephemeral injection queue (correspondent replies / recall notes); overflow drops the OLDEST with a WARN. Parity with the HITL queue's `MAX_QUEUED_MESSAGES` backpressure."),
    ("DEAD_TARGET_REGISTRY", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`true`", "Skip outbound sends to provably-dead targets (bot blocked / chat deleted), auto-revive on inbound from the target. Only suppresses definitively-classified failures; unknown errors unaffected. Note: revive is gated by this flag too — a mark set before a flag-OFF window survives i…"),
    ("EMAIL_SURFACE_ENABLED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (**ON for `polyrob email`**) (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Email surface (IMAP poll inbound + SMTP outbound). v1 is correspondent-only; owner-by-email stays OFF."),
    ("EMAIL_IMAP_POLL_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`60`", "Seconds between IMAP polls for new mail (no IDLE in v1)."),
    ("EMAIL_AUTONOMY_RUNTIME", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Whether `polyrob email` starts the shared autonomy runtime (goal dispatcher + cron ticker + curator + surface GC). Default OFF — the telegram process is the single autonomy driver, so a telegram-outbound goal can never be claimed by the email-only process (whose `MessageRouter`…"),
    ("API_AUTONOMY_RUNTIME", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "**ON**", "Whether the api process (`polyrob serve`) starts the shared autonomy loops. Default ON keeps the single-process posture intact; set OFF when the api runs ALONGSIDE another entrypoint on the same data dir — two runtimes mean two settlement watchers racing one `settlement_scan` ch…"),
    ("GMAIL_EMAIL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Mail credentials for the `email` tool (SMTP send + IMAP read) — the email surface reuses the same tool/creds. Both must be set or the email tool refuses to initialize. Any IMAP/SMTP provider works despite the `GMAIL_` name (see server vars below)."),
    ("GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Mail credentials for the `email` tool (SMTP send + IMAP read) — the email surface reuses the same tool/creds. Both must be set or the email tool refuses to initialize. Any IMAP/SMTP provider works despite the `GMAIL_` name (see server vars below)."),
    ("GMAIL_IMAP_SERVER", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`imap.gmail.com` / `smtp.gmail.com` / `587`", "IMAP/SMTP server endpoints for the email tool; point these at any provider."),
    ("GMAIL_SMTP_SERVER", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`imap.gmail.com` / `smtp.gmail.com` / `587`", "IMAP/SMTP server endpoints for the email tool; point these at any provider."),
